Z||000000||Ed||01-28-2001||01:02 PM||||Wahoo!!<P>I went to the "High Performance Street Car Driving School" at Thunderhill Park.  This is a facility of the San Francisco Region, SCCA. It is about 100 miles north of Sacramento, CA.<P>Every time I take my '87 GT out for a fast drive, I'm impressed with the car.  The only mod is a rear sway bar and front and rear plastic bar bushings.<P>Folks, the car is better than you are! Everyone wants to have more power and brakes, even the Porsche people.  But, to keep down the space on the board I'm not going to rant forever even though my adrenalin is still up.  Be happy with the (cheap) sports car you've got, and know that it performs just fine and go out there and have fun.  <P>P.S. If you're interested in going fast on winding roads, take driving lessons.  Its a zillion times more cost effective than just about anything (except maybe the rear bar!). <p>[This message has been edited by Ed (edited 01-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheHans||01-28-2001||03:48 PM||||How much was it?<P>Is there any of school like that around in Illinois.<BR>A friend of mine went to one of those before he started racing. He said it was awesome and well worth it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||01-28-2001||04:38 PM||||Mid Ohio in Lexington (north of Columbus) has one in spring and summer, dont know how far that is for you<P>Is there any of school like that around in Illinois.<BR>A friend of mine went to one of those before he started racing. He said it was awesome and well worth it.[/B][/QUOTE]<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ed||01-28-2001||05:48 PM||||It was $175.  For that you got a breakfast of coffee, juice, muffins, etc.  You got a light lunch of sandwich, drinks, etc., a sort of reception afterwards, and a T-shirt.<P>The driving part included lectures and track time.  The driving was with an instructor for several laps around the equivalent of three courses depending how they set up the track.  <BR>We were supposed to get five, 20 minute sessions, but because of the off-roading people were doing we lost one session to a lecture about safe driving.   <P>It definitely "was awesome and well worth it."<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Ed (edited 01-28-2001).]||||reg||1
